<article class="env-lemma" id="09BD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09BD">Lemma <span data-tag="09BD">21.53.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site with final object $X$. Let $\Lambda $ be a ring. Let </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$K$ a perfect object of $D(\Lambda )$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a finite complex $K^\bullet $ of finite projective $\Lambda $-modules representing $K$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{L}^\bullet $ a complex of sheaves of $\Lambda $-modules, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi : \underline{K} \to \mathcal{L}^\bullet $ a map in $D(\mathcal{C}, \Lambda )$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists a covering $\{ U_ i \to X\} $ and maps of complexes $\alpha _ i : \underline{K}^\bullet |_{U_ i} \to \mathcal{L}^\bullet |_{U_ i}$ representing $\varphi |_{U_ i}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/08FR" data-tag="08FR">21.44.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>